    body: "With the chat assistant you ask questions in your own words instead of clicking through lists, and sign in or out with one sentence. You find it as a coloured card at the top of “More” (in the new design under “Me”). It is still in beta.\n\n**You can ask:**\n- “How was my attendance in the last 3 months?”\n- “How often did Jonas come this year?”, “How was Jonas at talks?” or “What is the rate of the tenors?” (only [[Administrator|administrators]], [[Verantwortlicher|responsible persons]] and [[Helfer|helpers]])\n- “Who is coming on Sunday?”, “Who was there last Sunday?” or “Who hasn't answered for Wednesday yet?” (only leaders and helpers)\n- “When is the next rehearsal?” (for members across all instances)\n- “Who has a birthday this month?” (only leaders and helpers)\n- “When did we last sing ‘Holy God’?”\n- “How do I sign out?” (shows matching help articles)\n\n**You can change:**\n- Sign yourself in or out or report being late: “Sign me out for Sunday, I'm ill”, “I'll be late on Wednesday, traffic”, “Sign me out of everything next week”. Excused and late need a reason, like signing out in the app; if it is missing, the chat asks for it. This works across all your [[Instanz|instances]], like the overview. The same rules as in “My events” apply (deadline, registration fields), and the leaders of each instance are notified as usual.\n- Enter a planned absence: “I'm on holiday from 3 to 10 March”, if your role may do so.\n- As a leader or [[Helfer|helper]], set the status of others: “Jonas and Marie were there on Wednesday”, “Tenors excused on Sunday, choir retreat”. Leaders can also enter absences of others: “Lena is abroad until the end of January”.\n- As [[Elternteil|parents]], sign your children in or out: “Sign Lena out for Sunday, she is ill” or “My children will be late on Wednesday, doctor's appointment”. This only works for your own children and only for their upcoming events, with the same rules as in the parents area. Excused or late needs a reason here too, and the leaders are notified as usual.\n\n**Events (if you may create or edit events):**\n- Create events: “Create a rehearsal every Wednesday in December at 19:30”. At most 20 at once, from today up to 6 months ahead. Days that already have an event of this type get no second one. If there are several event types, it asks which one. You may create events in the chat if you may on the events page.\n- Move events: “Move the rehearsal on Wednesday to Thursday” or “The rehearsal on Sunday starts at 10”. This works like “Change date”: deadline and checklist move along, statuses stay, and anyone with an absence on the new day is excused.\n- Pieces for an event: “Put ‘Holy God’ and no. 12 on the rehearsal on Sunday”. The pieces are added; only if you say these are exactly the pieces does it replace the list.\n\n**Tasks, duties, people and messages:**\n- “Which pieces are we singing on Sunday?” shows the pieces of an event (members see the pieces of their own events).\n- “Which tasks are open for me?” lists your open tasks if team organisation is switched on.\n- Create a task: “Thomas sorts out the room by Friday” (only [[Administrator|administrators]] and [[Verantwortlicher|responsible persons]], with team organisation). Due date from today up to 6 months ahead. Thomas only gets a message when you tap “Notify” after saving.\n- Take over a duty: “I'll do the setup on Sunday”. This only works for yourself and like “I'll take it”: the duty must allow signing up yourself, you must belong to the duty team, and a place must still be free.\n- Add a person: “New member Anna Müller, soprano, birthday 3.4.2008” (only [[Administrator|administrators]] and [[Verantwortlicher|responsible persons]]). The chat saves nothing; it opens the normal “Add person” form with the details. You check everything there and save yourself.\n- Reminder or message: “Remind the tenors about Sunday” or “Write to everyone who hasn't answered for Wednesday” (only [[Administrator|administrators]] and [[Verantwortlicher|responsible persons]]). The chat only writes a draft with the event and your own words and opens the normal message page with it. Nothing is sent until you tap Send there yourself.\n\n**How it stays safe:** Before anything is saved, the chat shows exactly which events change, and you tap “Save” or “Cancel”. From 11 changes on it asks a second time. After saving you can take everything back with “Undo”. For new events, “Undo” deletes exactly the events just created. At most 30 status changes per message, only events from 14 days back to 6 months ahead, and absences from today up to 6 months ahead. The chat does not change archived events. Deleting events, people or tasks, changing roles or settings and sending messages directly is not possible in the chat. For a new task, “Undo” deletes exactly that task; for a duty you took over, you are free again afterwards. You can never change more than you can elsewhere in the app.\n\nIf several people have that name, the assistant asks whom you mean. You can write in German, English, Russian or Spanish.\n\n**Voice input:** Tap the microphone next to the input field and say your sentence. The text appears in the field, and it is only sent when you tap Send. On iPhone, iPad and Mac the device recognises speech itself; on Android and in the browser the speech service of the system or browser is used. The first time, the device asks for access to the microphone.\n\n**Switching it on:** An [[Administrator|administrator]] switches the assistant on per [[Instanz|instance]], under “More” › “Settings” › “Chat assistant (beta)” (in the new design under “Roles and rights” › “What members see”). Then everyone in the instance can use it.\n\n**Privacy:** Only your typed message goes to the AI service, together with today's date and the names of the groups and event types. People, attendance and other data do not leave Attendix: the app works out the answers itself, and you only see what you may see anyway. The chat is not stored. There is a daily limit per person and per instance.",
