    body: "In the members list each person shows their attendance in percent. By default it counts all events since the start of the season whose event type counts for the attendance rate. You can also see the rate for a shorter period or for one event type only, for example “This year” or only talks.\n\n**In the new design:** In “Members”, tap “Filter”. Under “Count attendance” choose “Season”, “This year”, “3 months”, “12 months” or “Custom …” for From and To. Below, at “Event type”, choose whether all counting events or only one event type count.\n\n**In the old design:** In the list of people, open the options menu next to the search. There you find the period (calendar icon) and the event type.\n\nThe percentages, the average per group (instrument or voice) and the sort by attendance then follow your choice. At the top the choice shows as “Rate: …”; in the new design you remove it with the X, in the old design you set “Season” and “All that count” again. If a person had no matching events in the chosen period, no number is shown. The choice is only for you and stays until you close the app or switch [[Instanz|instance]].\n\n[[Administrator|Administrators]], [[Verantwortlicher|responsible persons]] and [[Helfer|helpers]] see the list. You can also ask the chat assistant the same question, e.g. “How was the attendance of the tenors this year?”.",
